{"id": "EUVD-2026-81165", "enisaUuid": "07475ced-d64b-3dbb-bf81-5e91c9fc3516", "description": "A vulnerability in the Online Certificate Status Protocol (OCSP) responder of Cisco ISE and Cisco ISE-PIC could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause an administrative reload of the OCSP responder certificate and key material.\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to missing authentication on a function of the OCSP responder. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by sending a crafted request to an affected device. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to cause the OCSP responder to reload certificate and key material on demand.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T20:24:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-17T14:03:00", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:L", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-ise-multiauth-bypass-sgD2HbL4"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-76447", "GHSA-vwx3-phv6-wmxp"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00f0918e-e082-398b-b83b-ccd7b7406b54", "product": {"name": "Cisco ISE Passive Identity Connector", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.2.0"}, {"id": "01d76974-a620-3f94-ba45-105e43b9ab80", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.4 Patch 2"}, {"id": "03e29429-9359-3848-a86f-403df02e89ca", "product": {"name": "Cisco ISE Passive Identity Connector", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.0"}, {"id": "0ca97918-17bc-35b7-8dfd-51bacf725529", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.3.0"}, {"id": "0d6bad0d-06a3-3792-8d96-8eae344f19d7", "product": {"name": "Cisco Identity Services Engine Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.1.0 p5"}, {"id": "10743ed1-2f07-30de-80c2-10fefac153cd", "product": {"name